UPDATE public.client_plans SET frontend_plan_data = '[{"day":1,"title":"The Authority Shift","objective":"Signal a shift in your content strategy and establish your authority as someone who has mastered the balance of physical and mental structure. By asking for feedback, you make the audience feel involved in the creation process, which increases their future buy-in.","whyItMatters":"This day sets the foundation for the entire 14-day sequence. Without establishing authority and identifying the audience''s specific problems, the later sales pitches will feel cold and irrelevant.","actions":["Post a high-energy rugby training highlight reel or gym PR video. This grabs attention immediately because it showcases the aspirational result your audience wants.","In the caption, mention that you are shifting your focus to helping others achieve the same structure you use. This signals a transition from creator to coach which is vital for authority.","Ask a specific question in the comments: What is your biggest struggle with balancing gym and rugby? This identifies the pain points you will solve later."],"psychologicalLever":"The Commitment and Consistency principle. By asking the audience for their struggles, you are getting them to mentally commit to the idea that they have a problem that needs solving. This makes them more receptive to your solution later.","expectedOutcome":"High engagement and a list of specific audience pain points to address in the coming days.","contentIdeas":["A montage of rugby match footage followed by a heavy squat session.","A text-overlay video: How I went from confused in the gym to a structured pro routine."]},{"day":2,"title":"The Behind-the-Scenes Reality","objective":"Demonstrate Proof of Concept. You are showing that the structure you talk about is achievable for a busy person, which lowers the barrier to entry for your followers.","whyItMatters":"This day is critical because it humanizes the Pro persona. It leads to the Value phase by showing that your success is the result of a repeatable system, not just luck or genetics.","actions":["Share a Day in the Life story sequence showing your meal prep and workout planning.","Explain the Why behind one specific meal or exercise. This educates the audience and builds trust in your expertise.","Use a poll: Do you feel more lost with your training or your nutrition? This data helps you tailor your messaging."],"psychologicalLever":"Social Proof and Relatability. When people see that you face the same time constraints they do but have a system to overcome them, they begin to believe they can achieve similar results.","expectedOutcome":"A clear understanding of whether your audience struggles more with the physical or mental side of the game.","contentIdeas":["A photo of a structured weekly calendar next to a gym bag.","A quick video showing how you prep 3 days of rugby-specific fuel in 20 minutes."]},{"day":3,"title":"The Pattern Interrupt","objective":"Challenge the status quo and introduce the New Way of training. By debunking common myths, you position yourself as a thought leader who offers a unique solution.","whyItMatters":"This is the final day of the warmup. It transitions the audience from passive observers to active participants who are now waiting for a solution.","actions":["Post a Myth vs. Reality graphic regarding rugby fitness.","Explain that you are currently recording a Professional Program to solve these specific issues. This is the first soft mention of the product.","Ask people to Drop a rugby emoji if you want to see the curriculum. This builds a list of warm leads."],"psychologicalLever":"The Zeigarnik Effect. By mentioning a program is coming but not releasing it yet, you create a mental open loop that the audience will want to close.","expectedOutcome":"A list of high-intent followers who have raised their hands and expressed interest in a structured program.","contentIdeas":["A carousel: 3 Mistakes Rugby Players Make in the Gym.","A video explaining why just lifting heavy is not enough for on-field performance."]},{"day":4,"title":"The Value Drop: Nutrition","objective":"Provide massive upfront value. By giving away a piece of your expertise for free, you prove that your paid products will be worth the investment.","whyItMatters":"This day is critical because it proves your Peak Performance Meal Plan is based on solid science and practical experience.","actions":["Release a free Mini-Guide or a detailed post on The 3 Pillars of Rugby Nutrition.","Explain how this specific value ties into the Peak Performance Meal Plan. You are giving away the What but keeping the How for the paid product.","Encourage users to save the post for later. Saves are a high-value metric that tells the algorithm your content is important."],"psychologicalLever":"Reciprocity. When you give someone something of value for free, they feel a subconscious obligation to support you in return.","expectedOutcome":"Increased trust and Reciprocity from the audience as they receive high-quality information for free.","contentIdeas":["A detailed infographic showing the ideal pre-match meal timing.","A video: The one supplement every rugby player actually needs."]},{"day":5,"title":"The Value Drop: Consistency","objective":"Solve the Time objection before it even arises. By providing a home workout guide, you show that your system works regardless of the environment.","whyItMatters":"This day addresses the Consistency topic directly. It shows that your 7-Day Consistency Engine is the logical next step.","actions":["Share a specific 15-minute Home Workout that complements rugby training.","Explain why home workouts are essential for consistency when you cannot get to the gym.","Ask followers to tag a teammate who needs more consistency. This expands your reach."],"psychologicalLever":"The Foot-in-the-Door technique. By getting them to do a small, free 15-minute workout, you are making it much more likely they will commit to a full program later.","expectedOutcome":"Followers performing the workout and sharing their results, creating a community feel around your training methods.","contentIdeas":["A fast-paced Follow Along home workout video.","A text post: No gym? No problem. Do these 4 moves to stay rugby-ready."]},{"day":6,"title":"The Mindset Shift","objective":"Pivot from physical tactics to mental strategy. Most fitness creators only talk about muscles; by talking about Mindset coaching and Clarity, you differentiate yourself.","whyItMatters":"This day is critical because it addresses the Mindset coaching topic. It prepares the audience for the recorded professional program which includes these mental frameworks.","actions":["Post a video about the Rugby Mindset. Discuss how structure in the gym leads to clarity on the pitch.","Share a personal story of a time you lacked structure and how it negatively impacted your performance.","Ask: What is the one thing that stops you from being consistent? Use the replies to create Day 7 content."],"psychologicalLever":"Vulnerability and Liking. People buy from people they like and relate to. By sharing your own struggles, you become a peer who has found a way out.","expectedOutcome":"Deepened emotional connection with the audience and a better understanding of their mental barriers.","contentIdeas":["A Talking Head video: Why your brain is your most important muscle for rugby.","A quote card: Clarity in the mind, power in the gym."]},{"day":7,"title":"The Transformation Proof","objective":"Provide Logical Proof. After three days of value, you need to show the cumulative result of applying all these principles. This day acts as the bridge between Value and Launch.","whyItMatters":"This day is the Pivot Point. It moves the conversation from Here is some advice to Here is the system you can buy.","actions":["Create a Case Study or Transformation post. Show the Before (unstructured, tired, inconsistent) and the After (The Aspiring Pro).","Break down the EXACT steps taken to get from A to B. This makes the transformation feel attainable.","Announce that the Aspiring Pro Playbook bundle will be available in 3 days. This is the first official announcement."],"psychologicalLever":"The Halo Effect. By showing a successful transformation, the audience associates all your products with that success, making the bundle feel more valuable.","expectedOutcome":"A surge in anticipation and Save counts as people realize a comprehensive solution is coming.","contentIdeas":["A split-screen photo: Unstructured Training vs The Pro Playbook Method.","A carousel: How I gained 5kg of muscle and improved my sprint speed in 8 weeks."]},{"day":8,"title":"The Transparency Day","objective":"Remove Friction. By showing the inside of the product and answering questions, you eliminate the fear of the unknown.","whyItMatters":"This day is critical for converting skeptics into believers. It ensures the audience knows exactly what they are getting.","actions":["Host a Live Q&A session or a Question Box on stories. Answer questions about training, nutrition, and the upcoming program.","Show a Sneak Peek of the recorded program. Screen-record the members area or the PDF guides.","Explain the Early Bird bonus that will be available on launch day."],"psychologicalLever":"Risk Reduction. By showing exactly what is inside the program, you reduce the perceived risk of the purchase.","expectedOutcome":"Direct interaction with potential buyers and the clearing of any final doubts or objections.","contentIdeas":["A story slide: Everything inside the Aspiring Pro Playbook.","A Live video: Answering your rugby fitness questions."]},{"day":9,"title":"The Final Countdown","objective":"Create Anticipation. You are summarizing everything you have taught and positioning your product as the Ultimate Checklist for success.","whyItMatters":"This day is the Trigger. It ensures that when you post the link tomorrow, your audience is already primed and waiting to click.","actions":["Post a Final Checklist for rugby season prep. Include points that are covered in depth in your products.","Explain that tomorrow the doors open for the Aspiring Pro Playbook bundle at a special launch price.","Tell the audience to Turn on Post Notifications so they do not miss the link."],"psychologicalLever":"Anticipation. The human brain releases dopamine not just when receiving a reward, but in anticipation of it.","expectedOutcome":"High levels of Pre-Launch excitement and a large number of people setting reminders for the launch.","contentIdeas":["A checklist graphic: Are you actually ready for the season?","A countdown timer on stories: 18 hours until the Pro Playbook drops."]},{"day":10,"title":"The Launch: Doors Open","objective":"Conversion. After 9 days of building authority and value, you are now asking for the sale. The goal is to make the purchasing process as smooth and exciting as possible.","whyItMatters":"This is the Harvest day. All the work from the previous days culminates here. A successful Day 10 provides the social proof needed to carry the launch.","actions":["Post the Official Launch video. Clearly state what the product is, who it is for (Rugby players 15+), and where to get it.","Update your Bio link to the sales page. This is your primary Call to Action.","Share First Buyer shoutouts on stories. This creates immediate social proof."],"psychologicalLever":"Social Proof and Momentum. By highlighting the first few buyers, you create a bandwagon effect.","expectedOutcome":"A high volume of initial sales and a buzz across your social media profiles.","contentIdeas":["A cinematic trailer for The Aspiring Pro Playbook.","A Doors Open graphic with a clear list of the 3 products included in the bundle."]},{"day":11,"title":"The Deep Dive","objective":"Reinforcement. The initial excitement of launch day often dips; your goal today is to remind the audience why they need this program.","whyItMatters":"This day prevents the Mid-Launch Slump. It keeps the momentum going by providing new angles on the product.","actions":["Share a Deep Dive into one specific part of the program, like the 7-Day Consistency Engine.","Post a testimonial or a DM from someone who used your free tips and saw results.","Remind people that the Launch Discount or Bonus is still active but will not last forever."],"psychologicalLever":"The Unit Bias. By breaking the large Playbook down into smaller units, you make the overall program feel more achievable.","expectedOutcome":"Steady sales from people who were on the fence on Day 10.","contentIdeas":["A video: Why the first 7 days of this program are the most important.","A screenshot of a positive DM from a follower."]},{"day":12,"title":"The Objection Crusher","objective":"Objection Handling. Every potential customer has a reason not to buy. Today, you proactively address those reasons with logic and empathy.","whyItMatters":"This day is critical for capturing the late majority of your audience. It clears the path for the final Urgency phase.","actions":["Address the Top 3 Objections you have received in your DMs.","Explain that this program is specifically designed for the Aspiring Pro, regardless of their current starting point.","Use a This or That story poll to engage people, then link to the program as the solution."],"psychologicalLever":"Authority and Empathy. By answering questions directly, you reinforce your authority while showing you care about the individual.","expectedOutcome":"Conversion of the Analytical buyers who have specific questions that need answering before they commit.","contentIdeas":["A Green Screen video where you respond to common questions from your comments section.","A text post: 3 Reasons you have not reached your rugby potential yet."]},{"day":13,"title":"The Future Vision","objective":"Create Future Pacing. You want your audience to visualize their success after using your program. By combining this with the 24-hour warning, you create a powerful Push-Pull dynamic.","whyItMatters":"This day sets up the Grand Finale. It transitions the audience from I might buy this to I need to buy this before tomorrow.","actions":["Post a Results Recap. Show what someone can expect to achieve after 30 days of using the Playbook, Meal Plan, and Consistency Engine.","Announce that there are only 24 hours left to get the Launch Bundle price or bonuses.","Share a Thank You video to everyone who has joined so far."],"psychologicalLever":"Loss Aversion. People are more motivated to avoid losing an opportunity than they are to gain a benefit.","expectedOutcome":"A significant spike in sales as the procrastinators realize the opportunity is almost gone.","contentIdeas":["A Vision post: Imagine yourself 4 weeks from now: stronger, faster, and more focused.","A story with a large 24 HOURS LEFT countdown timer."]},{"day":14,"title":"The Final Call","objective":"Urgency. This is the final day to secure the launch deal. Your goal is to be everywhere in your followers feeds, reminding them that the window is closing.","whyItMatters":"This is the most critical day for your total revenue. Typically, 30-50% of launch sales happen in the final 24 hours.","actions":["Post 3-5 times on stories throughout the day. Use Last Chance messaging. 12 hours left, 6 hours left, 1 hour left.","Share one final Success Story or a powerful Why behind the program.","Post a Final Call grid post with a clear, bold image: DOORS CLOSING: The Aspiring Pro Playbook."],"psychologicalLever":"Scarcity (FOMO). The Fear Of Missing Out is at its peak on the final day. When something is about to become unavailable, its perceived value skyrockets.","expectedOutcome":"The highest sales day of the entire launch, driven by extreme urgency and the fear of missing out.","contentIdeas":["A series of Countdown stories with direct links to the checkout page.","A final Personal Message video: I do not want you to miss out on the structure you need for next season."]}]'::jsonb WHERE access_code = 'LAUNCH-GV79ER';